WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.460
- Our next guest, y'all,
is a perfect person

00:00:02.460 --> 00:00:04.860
to shine a light on For Giving Tuesday.

00:00:04.860 --> 00:00:08.010
With more than 17 million
followers on TikTok alone,

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:09.930
he is blown up on social media

00:00:09.930 --> 00:00:12.450
with videos of him
surprising complete strangers

00:00:12.450 --> 00:00:15.510
with gestures of love and appreciation.

00:00:15.510 --> 00:00:18.460
This summer, I teamed up with
him for one of these moments.

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.020
- Oh my gosh, nice to see you.

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:24.664
We're surprising you with Vegas.

00:00:24.664 --> 00:00:26.456
I don't know if you wanna
come to Vegas to see the show.

00:00:26.456 --> 00:00:27.289
(shouting)

00:00:27.289 --> 00:00:29.517
Hope you love the show!

00:00:29.517 --> 00:00:32.056
Ah, it was so cool to be a part of.

00:00:32.056 --> 00:00:35.910
Let's welcome Zach, known
on TikTok as MD Motivator.

00:00:35.910 --> 00:00:37.707
Welcome to the show.

00:00:37.707 --> 00:00:38.851
- Thank you for having me.

00:00:38.851 --> 00:00:41.580
- Absolutely, I love,
I'm obviously, you know,

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:44.040
I'm a fan of what you do, but
how did you get into this?

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:45.030
- [Zach] So the name on social media

00:00:45.030 --> 00:00:46.770
stands for MD Motivator,

00:00:46.770 --> 00:00:48.780
which means Medical Doctor Motivator

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:51.120
'cause during the COVID,
COVID and the pandemic,

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:52.729
I was in medical school
in Sydney, Australia.

00:00:52.729 --> 00:00:53.562
- Yeah.

00:00:53.562 --> 00:00:55.110
- And when I say the
pandemic, a lot of people

00:00:55.110 --> 00:00:56.790
really lacked connection and felt alone

00:00:56.790 --> 00:00:59.010
and during that time I had a con,

00:00:59.010 --> 00:01:01.110
a combination of things
that happened to me.

00:01:01.110 --> 00:01:02.760
I went through a six year
relationship breakup.

00:01:02.760 --> 00:01:04.320
Medical school was challenging.

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:05.520
I had an ACL surgery.

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.260
There wasn't anything particular-

00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:08.280
- Oh God, you didn't get a break.

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:09.690
- [Zach] But it was just a breaking point.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:10.523
- Yeah.

00:01:10.523 --> 00:01:11.610
- And it was finally a time in my life

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:13.470
where I saw a blank slate.

00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:14.303
Who am I?

00:01:14.303 --> 00:01:15.240
What's my purpose?

00:01:15.240 --> 00:01:16.080
What makes me happy?

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:17.880
And I just didn't feel,

00:01:17.880 --> 00:01:20.370
I was really in a hole and
I had no one to turn to.

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:22.320
So I started making videos

00:01:22.320 --> 00:01:24.652
to find a friend to create connection.

00:01:24.652 --> 00:01:25.485
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:26.318
- And that's how this journey started

00:01:26.318 --> 00:01:28.620
and I started making
blindfolded hugging videos

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:29.850
where I would hug strangers

00:01:29.850 --> 00:01:30.683
because one night

00:01:30.683 --> 00:01:32.820
when I was in Sydney,
Australia in medical school,

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:34.740
in the middle of the
night, I went for a walk.

00:01:34.740 --> 00:01:36.870
I didn't wanna tell my roommate
what I was going through

00:01:36.870 --> 00:01:38.220
and I sat there in the rain

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:39.750
and these two women in
their late thirties,

00:01:39.750 --> 00:01:42.210
they came up to me and they're
like, "What's going on?"

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:44.550
And I was like hysterically
crying at the time

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:45.420
and I said nothing

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:48.120
and they just sat there in the wet cement

00:01:48.120 --> 00:01:49.467
and they listened to me

00:01:49.467 --> 00:01:52.200
and the power of just
having a stranger hear me

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.790
made me wanna do that for others,

00:01:53.790 --> 00:01:56.190
so that's why I started
blindfolded hugging strangers

00:01:56.190 --> 00:01:58.170
if they're going through
depression or heartbroken

00:01:58.170 --> 00:01:59.760
or felt empty or missing someone.

00:01:59.760 --> 00:02:00.621
I just want-

00:02:00.621 --> 00:02:01.454
- Yeah.

00:02:01.454 --> 00:02:02.287
- [Zach] 'Cause that pivoted my life

00:02:02.287 --> 00:02:03.809
and I had never been able
to reach them ever again.

00:02:03.809 --> 00:02:04.642
- Wow.

00:02:04.642 --> 00:02:06.270
- So if you're listening out
there in Sydney, Australia,

00:02:06.270 --> 00:02:07.103
I love you.

00:02:07.103 --> 00:02:08.160
You've changed my life forever

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.866
and I just wanted to be the same for them.

00:02:09.866 --> 00:02:11.880
- [Kelly] Oh my, what a magical start?

00:02:11.880 --> 00:02:12.713
I'm not-

00:02:12.713 --> 00:02:13.603
- Yeah.

00:02:13.603 --> 00:02:14.436
- I didn't know that's how it started.

00:02:14.436 --> 00:02:15.269
- That's how it started.

00:02:15.269 --> 00:02:17.100
- Well what, what was your first video?

00:02:17.100 --> 00:02:20.250
- My first video was a
poster in September of 2021.

00:02:20.250 --> 00:02:22.110
